    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0502" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7452b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-27T22:00:00-04:00">March 27, 1942—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>231. Reference second paragraph Department’s 216, March 25, 11 p.m.<anchor
                        n="19a" xml:id="d377-f1"/> The Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs has
                    requested that his letter of March 21 to the Secretary of the Treasury be
                    amended to include a phrase to the effect that the channel through which the
                    Chinese Government would keep the Secretary of the Treasury informed would be
                    the Chinese Minister of Finance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
